{"data": {"acceptance": ["document rendering joins a single LF inside a paragraph into one space, so 'the evacuation\\ndropships were late' becomes 'the evacuation dropships were late'", "blank-line paragraph boundaries and form-feed page markers survive unwrapping unchanged", "a line ending in a hyphen joins with no space and keeps the hyphen, so 'mind-\\nnumbing' becomes 'mind-numbing'", "a trailing LF at the end of the document is not turned into a space", "gates pass: uv run --directory 04_Software/AudioMancer pytest -q and uv run --directory 04_Software/AudioMancer ruff check ."], "assumptions": [], "created_at": "2026-07-27T05:54:44+00:00", "decision": "proceed", "open_questions": [], "planned_paths": [], "reason": "Single deterministic post-pass over rendered document text in one service; auditable cleanup decisions in cleanup.json are untouched, the user picked this location and the hyphen policy explicitly, and backward compatibility for existing cleanup artifacts was waived.", "recommended_responses": [], "risk": "low", "scope": ["04_Software/AudioMancer/src/audiomancer/services/ai_cleanup_service.py, 04_Software/AudioMancer/tests/test_ai_cleanup_contract.py, .agentic/requirements/functional/, .agentic/knowledge/components/Text_Cleanup.md"], "source": "Chat 2026-07-27: user reported AI translation mirroring mid-sentence line breaks; root cause is AI Cleanup. User chose to unwrap only in AI Cleanup at document render, and to join hyphen-terminated wraps without a space while keeping the hyphen.", "understanding": "AI-assisted cleanup retains story slices byte-exact, so single LF characters that PDF extraction inserts at every wrapped line survive into clean_text.txt, chunks_text.json, the translation prompt, and TTS. Deterministic cleanup already unwraps these through _compose_paragraph_text, so the two cleanup modes disagree. Document rendering must join intra-paragraph line breaks into single spaces while keeping blank-line paragraph boundaries and form-feed page markers intact."}, "event": "alignment.recorded", "time": "2026-07-27T05:54:44+00:00"}
